Aether: the new settings page

Redesign toggles, fine-grained switches, standalone skeleton, button reroute, design switch, media/gamepad/motion shields, samplerate, intl coherence, battery/connection absences, geometry layer, standard/strict split, copy and presets, standard defaults, profile radios.

Squashed from 17 units:

  [core/133-settings-redesign-toggles.patch]
  Aether: render the Settings toggles in the settings redesign
  
  Aether: render the Settings toggles in the settings redesign
  
  The six fingerprinting switches lived only in the legacy template UI, which
  is never stamped while browser.settings-redesign.enabled is on (our default
  since the shields work): Privacy & Security showed nothing of ours. They are
  now a first-class setting group in the redesign infrastructure: one
  Preferences.addSetting binding per kill/opt-in pref, an aetherProtections
  group of moz-checkbox controls registered right after the ETP status card,
  and human descriptions on every label. The legacy groupbox stays untouched
  as the fallback if the redesign is ever off. Verified visually headless with
  a tall viewport screenshot plus a clean chrome log.
  
  [core/134-fine-grained-switches.patch]
  Aether: fine-grained fingerprint switches with a master toggle
  
  Aether: fine-grained fingerprint switches with a master toggle
  
  Six switches hid the real breadth: canvas, WebGL, audio, cores and text
  noise had kill prefs but no UI, and there was no master switch at all. The
  aetherProtections group now lists every layer individually behind its own
  switch, with the master first: canvas/audio/text/WebGL noise, core count,
  touch, fonts, languages, depth, UTC opt-in, fingerprinter blocking, plus the
  two stock opt-ins (WebGPU allow, UA token) bound directly with no engine
  change. The legacy template fallback mirrors the full list. Verified
  visually headless with a tall viewport screenshot plus a clean chrome log.
  
  [core/135-standalone-settings-skeleton.patch]
