  static skeleton ported from the user's mockup (layout, variable sets for
  all three themes, the sixteen icons, dashboard cards, quick cards, featured
  banner, section stub). Deliberately not ported: the remote webfont (offline
  rule, system stack instead), all scripts (theme/accent switching, search
  filter, section navigation, FPS meter) and the Spanish copy (public content
  is en-US). Registered in the about redirector (untrusted-content, hidden
  from about:about, child process, no script flag) and packaged through
  browser.jar. Not linked from anywhere yet; content gets built from the old
  menu unit by unit as directed. Revision (user direction): the header tools
  are out — no FPS meter (the FPS note always meant UI fluidity matched to
  the screen refresh, a standing principle, not a meter), no theme segmented
  control and no accent swatches here (not these four colors either — the
  real set is Light/Dark/Purple, placed elsewhere when the theme work
  lands). The theme/accent variable machinery stays inert in the
  stylesheet.
  
  
  Second step of the independent settings menu. The Appearance section is a
  big box holding small menu boxes; the first one is Browser color: three
  theme cards in a row, each wearing its own theme colors through per-card
  variable scoping, with the active card marked by an accent ring plus a new
